CORE
main.c
--no-por --unwind 2 --rounds 2
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
--
^split small choices
^warning: ignoring
--
The rest of t after the choice of i allocates: a split would give each copy
its own allocation site and multiply the heap objects, so t is not split.
i == 1 stores the new pointer in slot[1], failing the assertion.
